# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
#
# VM test (ci/test-install, 0.0.4.3 step 5, docs/decisions.md D112), on the serial console of an
# installed system: on its first boot, create the first account as a person would; the system
# fetches its extensions and reboots. On the next boot, wait until the check unit reported the
# extensions, then log in with the new account. Its shell is homed's default,
# beamline-shell, which only explains how to get a shell (D62). Never part of an image.

expect Please enter user name to create
sleep 1
send owner\n
expect Please enter new password for user owner:
sleep 1
send owner\n
expect \(repeat\):
sleep 1
send owner\n
expect BEAMLINE_FIRSTBOOT_CHECKED
# A fresh login prompt, in case the getty printed its own before the report.
sleep 2
send \n
expect [a-z0-9-]+ login:
send owner\n
expect Password:
send owner\n
expect does not enable an interactive login shell
